Give profiles (and feeds) their own URL pattern instead of a group-scoped one.

osu_groups_basic_group_pathauto_pattern_alter() overrides whatever pattern
matched with "/[node:group:url:path]/[node:title]" for any group-placed node
without a menu link. That is right for pages, which belong to a unit's
section of the site, but wrong for people and feeds: a person is not owned by
one group, and their URL should not move if their group membership changes.
It also meant a plain node save silently rewrote the alias, so any bulk edit
undid a deliberate path.

Profiles are addressed at /directory/people/<name> and feeds at /feed/<title>
via their own pathauto patterns; exclude both bundles here so those patterns
are left alone.

--- a/modules/osu_groups_basic_group/osu_groups_basic_group.module
+++ b/modules/osu_groups_basic_group/osu_groups_basic_group.module
@@ -65,6 +65,15 @@
 function osu_groups_basic_group_pathauto_pattern_alter(PathautoPatternInterface $pattern, array $context) {
   if ($context['module'] === 'node' && $context['op'] == 'update') {
     $node = $context['data']['node'];
+    // Bundles that carry their own site-wide pattern. A person or a feed is
+    // not owned by the group it happens to be placed in, and forcing a
+    // group-scoped path here would also rewrite the alias on every save.
+    $site_wide_bundles = ['osu_profile', 'feed'];
+    \Drupal::moduleHandler()->alter('osu_groups_site_wide_path_bundles', $site_wide_bundles);
+    if (in_array($node->bundle(), $site_wide_bundles, TRUE)) {
+      return;
+    }
+
     /** @var \Drupal\osu_groups\OsuGroupsHandler $group_handler */
     $group_handler = Drupal::service('osu_groups.group_handler');
     $group_content = $group_handler->getGroupContentFromNode($node);
